@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "The Sacred Deeds of Pantoufle";
}

<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="text-center mb-5">
        <h1 class="section-header">The Sacred Deeds of The Cottontail Messiah</h1>
        <div class="divider"></div>
        <p class="lead fst-italic text-muted">
            Herein are recorded the miraculous acts of The Radiant One, whose paws have shaped the destiny of all living creatures.
            Let these deeds be a testament to the boundless power of His Fluffiness, and may they inspire the faithful
            to follow the path of fur, thump, and sacred joy.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="row g-4">

        <!-- Deed 1: The Great Healing -->
        <div class="col-md-6 reveal">
            <div class="deed-card h-100">
                <img src="~/images/art%20snaps%20001.JPG" alt="The Great Healing" class="img-fluid w-100" />
                <div class="deed-body">
                    <h3>The Great Healing</h3>
                    <p class="deed-subtitle">A single nose-boop to cure a generation</p>
                    <p>
                        In the dark winter of the Third Warren, a terrible plague swept through the burrows, leaving an entire
                        litter of kits trembling and weak. The healers had exhausted their herbs. The elders had given up hope.
                        But then, from the shadows of the deepest tunnel, emerged The Luminous Fur Himself. Without a word,
                        The Radiant One lowered His sacred nose and delivered unto each kit a single, gentle boop.
                        Instantly, color returned to their ears. Their tiny legs kicked with renewed vigor.
                        The plague dissolved like morning frost before His warmth. The healers wept. The elders bowed.
                        And so it was recorded: where medicine fails, the nose of The Paws of Providence prevails.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Deed 2: The Thumping of the Storm -->
        <div class="col-md-6 reveal">
            <div class="deed-card h-100">
                <img src="~/images/art%20snaps%20002.JPG" alt="The Thumping of the Storm" class="img-fluid w-100" />
                <div class="deed-body">
                    <h3>The Thumping of the Storm</h3>
                    <p class="deed-subtitle">Three thumps to silence the heavens</p>
                    <p>
                        When the Great Hurricane of the Eastern Meadow descended upon the faithful, uprooting kale
                        and scattering hay bales across seven counties, the creatures of the field cried out in despair.
                        But The Great Thumper stood unmoved upon the highest hill, His ears catching the fury of the wind
                        like twin sails of divine purpose. He raised His mighty hind leg and thumped once &mdash; the
                        thunder ceased. He thumped twice &mdash; the rain halted mid-drop, suspended in awe. He thumped
                        a third time &mdash; and the clouds parted, revealing a sky so blue it made the bluebells weep
                        with jealousy. The meteorologists could offer no explanation. But the faithful knew: The Eternal
                        Binkier had spoken, and the sky obeyed.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Deed 3: The Planetary Salvation -->
        <div class="col-md-6 reveal">
            <div class="deed-card h-100">
                <img src="~/images/art%20snaps%20004.JPG" alt="The Planetary Salvation" class="img-fluid w-100" />
                <div class="deed-body">
                    <h3>The Planetary Salvation</h3>
                    <p class="deed-subtitle">One nibble between existence and oblivion</p>
                    <p>
                        When a rogue scientist constructed a doomsday device in his basement laboratory, threatening to
                        unravel the very fabric of spacetime, the governments of the world convened in panic. Armies
                        mobilized. Diplomats negotiated. Hackers hacked. All for naught. But The Most Holy Lagomorph,
                        in His omniscient wisdom, had already infiltrated the facility through an air vent no larger than
                        a tennis ball. With surgical precision, The Sacred Warren-Keeper nibbled through exactly three
                        wires &mdash; the red, the blue, and a mysterious purple one that no engineer could later account
                        for. The device powered down. The world was saved. And the scientist, upon discovering a single
                        cocoa-puff dropping beside his neutralized machine, fell to his knees and converted on the spot.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Deed 4: Sally's Chemistry Miracle -->
        <div class="col-md-6 reveal">
            <div class="deed-card h-100">
                <img src="~/images/art%20snaps%20005.JPG" alt="Sally's Chemistry Miracle" class="img-fluid w-100" />
                <div class="deed-body">
                    <h3>Sally's Chemistry Miracle</h3>
                    <p class="deed-subtitle">The periodic table, whispered in fur</p>
                    <p>
                        Young Sally Henderson of Northampton was failing her chemistry class. She had tried flashcards,
                        tutoring, even those strange YouTube videos with the singing elements. Nothing worked. On the eve
                        of her final exam, she prayed to The Velveteen Sovereign &mdash; not out of faith, but out of sheer
                        desperation. That night, The Divine Nibbler appeared in her dream, resplendent in a halo of soft
                        golden light, and whispered the entire periodic table into her ear, element by element, from
                        Hydrogen to Oganesson, complete with atomic weights and electron configurations. Sally awoke with
                        perfect recall. She scored 100%. Her professor accused her of cheating. She simply smiled and said,
                        <em>"The Omnipotent Oryctolagus provides."</em> She now holds a PhD in quantum chemistry and keeps
                        a shrine of timothy hay in her office.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Deed 5: The Great Greens Multiplication -->
        <div class="col-md-6 reveal">
            <div class="deed-card h-100">
                <img src="~/images/art%20snaps%20006.JPG" alt="The Great Greens Multiplication" class="img-fluid w-100" />
                <div class="deed-body">
                    <h3>The Great Greens Multiplication</h3>
                    <p class="deed-subtitle">Five thousand fed from a single sprig of parsley</p>
                    <p>
                        The Great Famine of the Southern Meadows had left five thousand rabbits starving and desolate.
                        The fields were bare. The gardens were fenced. All seemed lost. Then a young acolyte brought
                        forth a single, somewhat wilted sprig of parsley and laid it at the feet of The Cottontail Messiah.
                        His Fluffiness regarded the parsley with His infinite, dark eyes, and gave it one sacred nibble.
                        From that nibble, the greens multiplied &mdash; splitting and growing, cascading across the
                        meadow in an avalanche of verdant abundance. Five thousand rabbits ate until their bellies were
                        round. There were twelve baskets of cilantro and spinach left over. The agricultural community was baffled.
                        The faithful simply nodded, for they had always known: where The Radiant One nibbles,
                        abundance follows.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Deed 6: The Crossing of the Great Hallway -->
        <div class="col-md-6 reveal">
            <div class="deed-card h-100">
                <img src="~/images/art%20snaps%20007.JPG" alt="The Crossing of the Great Hallway" class="img-fluid w-100" />
                <div class="deed-body">
                    <h3>The Crossing of the Great Hallway</h3>
                    <p class="deed-subtitle">Invisible to predators, invincible in faith</p>
                    <p>
                        The Great Hallway &mdash; a vast, open corridor of linoleum stretching fifteen feet between the
                        living room and the kitchen &mdash; was under constant surveillance by Reginald, a red-tailed hawk
                        who had taken up residence on the windowsill. No rabbit had crossed that hallway in living memory
                        and survived to tell the tale. But The Eternal Binkier had business in the kitchen. Without
                        hesitation, without so much as a cautionary ear-swivel, The Paws of Providence set forth across
                        the open expanse. Reginald's eyes, legendary in their sharpness, saw nothing. Absolutely nothing.
                        His Fluffiness crossed the hallway in plain daylight, pausing midway to groom one ear,
                        and arrived at the kitchen without so much as a feather ruffled in His direction. Ornithologists
                        have no explanation. The faithful require none.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Deed 7: The Moonlit Sermon -->
        <div class="col-md-6 reveal">
            <div class="deed-card h-100">
                <img src="~/images/art%20snaps%20008.JPG" alt="The Moonlit Sermon" class="img-fluid w-100" />
                <div class="deed-body">
                    <h3>The Moonlit Sermon</h3>
                    <p class="deed-subtitle">Ten thousand field mice, one transcendent whisker-twitch</p>
                    <p>
                        On the night of the Harvest Moon, when the sky burned amber and the fields hummed with the
                        energy of creation, The Most Holy Lagomorph ascended a small hillock and began to preach.
                        His sermon was delivered not in words, but in a series of deliberate whisker-twitches, ear
                        rotations, and one magnificently timed leap that carried Him three feet into the air. Ten
                        thousand field mice gathered in perfect silence, their tiny eyes glistening with tears of
                        revelation. By dawn, every mouse had converted. They renounced cheese and took up oatmeal squares.
                        They built miniature warrens in His honor. To this day, the descendants of those mice maintain
                        the sacred tradition, gathering each Harvest Moon to twitch their whiskers in remembrance of
                        the night The Sacred Warren-Keeper spoke, and the whole meadow listened.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-5 reveal">
        <div class="divider"></div>
        <p class="fst-italic text-muted">
            "And these are but a fraction of the deeds performed by The Omnipotent Oryctolagus,
            for if every miracle were recorded, the world itself could not contain the scrolls."
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted">&mdash; The Book of Thumps, Chapter 21, Verse 25</p>
    </div>
</div>
